  "qualified_claim": "For the four frozen O14 pre-cap profiles, the 1 cm surface-cap event under 12*KSAT supply can be detected and localized from the committed physical state without A4/A8 event-root seeds, full-interval predictor trajectories or trajectory-bisection search. One initial surface-face evaluation supplies a physical tau seed and one constrained event corrector converges to the independently qualified A8 cap event with mass, state and face-accuracy diagnostics far inside the frozen gates. For the twelve frozen lower-supply controls, a conservative zero-infiltration upper bound proves the cap cannot be reached within the 0.05 d interval, so no nonlinear solve is performed.",
  "decision": "QUALIFIED_RESTRICTED_SEED_FREE_O14_SURFACE_CAP_EVENT_DETECTION_READY_FOR_CAP_GENERALIZATION_AND_EVENT_DETECTOR_ROBUSTNESS_RESEARCH",
  "architecture_checks": {
    "compact_state": "No detector or event-time persistence is added.",
    "scratch": "tau seed and event corrector are worker-local.",
    "transactionality": "Candidate event state remains scratch until accepted; synthetic reject and all no-event controls preserve original committed state and zero runoff ledger.",
    "generic_time": "tau is an offset inside the explicit 0.05 d interval.",
    "mass_conservation": "Worst candidate event balance residual is 4.30e-15 cm; no repair or clipping.",
    "bounded_cost": "One event corrector for positive cases; zero nonlinear solves for algebraically impossible controls; no full-trajectory event search.",
    "runtime_composition": "Detector composes surface ledger and soil/face contracts outside the Ross face kernel."
  },
  "hard_nonclaims": [
    "No generic bracket discovery for inconclusive cases where the direct physical seed/corrector fails.",
    "No surface-cap generalization beyond 1 cm.",
    "No material other than O14.",
    "No top-node h=0 saturation-event qualification.",
    "No response tangent through event detection.",
    "No production implementation, runtime, MultiSWAP, MODFLOW or groundwater admission."
  ],
